window.docContents[54].resolve({"/#A-Property-Kind-Calculus-for-Metrology___-proving-quantity-and-unit-laws-in-Lean___-from-ISO___IEC-80000-to-measurement-uncertainty--Onboarding___-Human-Context-Protocols--L1-___-Two-bodies--Pull":{"contents":"Two bodies are now in view, one inside each black-box oscillator: whose mass is this? Bare reals and bearer-free kinded values let one oscillator's mass enter another's formula. L1 indexes mass and stiffness by an oscillator bearer scoped to a nominal Rig, so its own k/m is accepted and cross-oscillator operations are refused. Each oscillator is the whole characterized by ω₀, which is why k and m share its index. One name is one system: records under that name are its states at different times, configurations, or rival estimates of it; comparing them is the point. Different names, R₁ and R₂, are distinct systems even when their parameters match. L2 opens each box into body and spring(s), revisits which component bears mass and stiffness, and considers the pair as a whole.\n\n","context":"A Property Kind Calculus for Metrology: proving quantity and unit laws in Lean, from ISO/IEC 80000 to measurement uncertainty\u0009Onboarding: Human Context Protocols\u0009L1 — Two bodies","header":"5.2.3. Pull","id":"/#A-Property-Kind-Calculus-for-Metrology___-proving-quantity-and-unit-laws-in-Lean___-from-ISO___IEC-80000-to-measurement-uncertainty--Onboarding___-Human-Context-Protocols--L1-___-Two-bodies--Pull"},"/#A-Property-Kind-Calculus-for-Metrology___-proving-quantity-and-unit-laws-in-Lean___-from-ISO___IEC-80000-to-measurement-uncertainty--Write-Once___-Correctly--The-five-steps":{"contents":"\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n","context":"A Property Kind Calculus for Metrology: proving quantity and unit laws in Lean, from ISO/IEC 80000 to measurement uncertainty\u0009Write Once, Correctly","header":"18.1. The five steps","id":"/#A-Property-Kind-Calculus-for-Metrology___-proving-quantity-and-unit-laws-in-Lean___-from-ISO___IEC-80000-to-measurement-uncertainty--Write-Once___-Correctly--The-five-steps"}});